# Cursor Project Rules for Portfolio Website
# This file helps maintain context across chat sessions

## Project Overview
- Single page portfolio website built with Next.js, TypeScript, and shadcn/ui
- Dark/light theme support with focus on performance and accessibility
- Following the PRD specifications for a high-performance landing page

## Code Style & Conventions
- Use TypeScript for type safety
- Follow React best practices with Next.js App Router architecture
- Prefer functional components with hooks
- Use shadcn/ui components with custom styling
- Maintain responsive design (mobile-first approach)

## Git Commit Message Standards
- Use conventional commit format: <type>(<scope>): <description>
- Types:
  - feat: New features
  - fix: Bug fixes
  - docs: Documentation changes
  - style: Code style changes (formatting, missing semicolons, etc.)
  - refactor: Code changes that neither fix bugs nor add features
  - perf: Performance improvements
  - test: Adding or modifying tests
  - chore: Changes to build process, auxiliary tools, libraries

## Project Structure
- `/src/app`: Next.js App Router pages and layouts
- `/src/components`: Reusable React components
- `/src/components/sections`: Page section components
- `/src/components/ui`: UI components from shadcn/ui
- `/src/lib`: Utility functions and helpers
- `/public`: Static assets (images, fonts, etc.)

## Important Notes
- The site follows a dark-first design with light theme toggle
- Email addresses and social links need to be replaced with actual data
- Performance is a priority (target Lighthouse score 95+)
- Accessibility features are crucial (ARIA labels, keyboard navigation)
- Analytics events are set up for key user interactions

